            "review_title": "Review at Eugene Cake Shop",
            "review_text": "Christopher B\nGarland, Texas12 contributions\n0\nA sweet treat\nFeb 2014 • Friends\nThe Japanese purin is addictive! At under $1.50 usd it is an affordable splurge. It is served chilled in small glass jars that are the perfect size to not feel guilty after eating such a decadent treat! \nLocated next door to Cyclo Resto a popular restaurant and cooking school and down the street from the Galaxy Cinema in the heart of District 1. This cute little shop also sells hand made clothing, cloth key chains, headbands and bags along with a few other handmade items. \nThe staff is very friendly and gave us advice about a local beach and how to avoid tourist traps. I look forward to trying other treats on their menu but can't help myself from trying every flavor of purin.\nRead more\nService\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 19, 2014",
